# Repo conventions

Follow `docs/repo-conventions.md`. Code style is `docs/coding-conventions.md`.

## Layout

- `src/prism/` — Python (schema, ingest, pipeline, pointers, publish)
- `src/cms/` — Astro citizen site (`package.json` lives here)
- `tests/` — tests
- `docs/` — verdicts, charters, conventions; kebab-case filenames
- `docs/personas/` — agent personas (see `docs/team.md`)
- `data/` — downloaded / generated data (gitignored except `.gitkeep`)
- `logs/` — experiment output (gitignored except `.gitkeep`)

New docs go under `docs/` with kebab-case names. STOP memos and closed-programme summaries belong in `docs/archive/`; active next work in `docs/next/`.

Do not invent extra top-level folders (`apps/`, `packages/`, `web/`). Citizen pages are generated from templates plus a data vintage — not a source of truth in a new top-level folder.

Tooling is locked in `docs/repo-conventions.md`: one repo; Python under `src/prism/`; Astro SSG under `src/cms/`; `pyproject.toml` at root. Do not add Next.js, ISR, or a request-time producer fetch.
